{%- comment -%}
  PG Save Badge: make the SAVE % badge on every offer tile the first thing read.

  pg-theme-css draws it small and dark:

      .pgx-lad-badge{font-size:11.5px;font-weight:800;padding:5px 14px;
                     background:#0D0714;color:#fff;border:1px solid rgba(139,68,190,.6)}

  On a near-black tile on a near-black page that is a dark pill on a dark card —
  the number a shopper is meant to see first is the quietest thing in the tile.
  What makes it read now is the CONTRAST, not the size: it is filled rather than
  hollow, and the type is only a step up from the original (12.5px vs 11.5px). A
  first pass at 14px/900 with the padding to match was called out as far too big
  — the pill sits half over the tile's top edge, so it grows into the tile above
  it rather than into empty space.

  IT BELONGS TO THE TILE'S FRAME. A second pass used the add-to-cart buttons'
  bright gradient (#B478E0 -> #7A2FA2) with a white hairline and a coloured
  glow, and read as a sticker dropped on the card rather than part of it. The
  fill is now the deep end of the same purple family — the tile border's own
  #7A2FA2 into #4A1C66 — the hairline is that border's colour instead of white,
  and the glow is a plain soft shadow. The gradient stays, so the pill still has
  depth and still separates from the flat tile behind it; it just sits in the
  frame the tile already draws.

  One rule covers every tile on every product: pgLadder's ladder tiles, pgDuo's
  Duo Pack ([data-pg-duosave]) and pg-landing's single tile
  ([data-pg-singlesave]) all render the badge with this class.

  Registered in sections/header-group.json, which renders before pg-theme-css in
  the footer group — so these are stamped !important and id-scoped to outrank it
  on specificity rather than on source order.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
  html body #pgx .pgx-lad-badge{
    background:linear-gradient(120deg,#8B44BE 0%,#7A2FA2 45%,#4A1C66 100%) !important;
    color:#F7EDFF !important;
    font-family:'Poppins','Segoe UI',Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif !important;
    font-size:12.5px !important;
    font-weight:800 !important;
    letter-spacing:.04em !important;
    padding:5px 13px !important;
    border:1px solid rgba(139,68,190,.85) !important;
    box-shadow:0 6px 14px -10px rgba(0,0,0,.85) !important;
    text-shadow:none !important;
    text-transform:uppercase !important;
    white-space:nowrap !important;
  }
  @media (max-width:600px){
    html body #pgx .pgx-lad-badge{font-size:12px !important;padding:5px 11px !important}
  }
</style>
{% schema %}
{"name": "PG Save Badge", "settings": [], "presets": [{"name": "PG Save Badge"}]}
{% endschema %}
